{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 87, :comments ["<b>All the cattle for burnt-offering.</b> This offering of the princes at the dedication of the altar was twelve bulls, twelve rams, twelve lambs, twelve goats, corresponding to the twelve tribes above." "<b>And you already</b> know that the Glory that descended upon Mount Sinai was transferred to the Tabernacle: just as it descended on Mount Sinai with the banners of the ministering angels, so Israel, when the Tabernacle set out, were arranged in banners. Just as He bounded Mount Sinai and said (Exodus 19:13) ״לא תגע בו יד״, so He bounded the Tabernacle (Numbers 1:51) — ״והזר הקרב יומת״. And so the matter here: when the dedication of the altar was completed and the Tabernacle was erected, they offered twelve offerings corresponding to what was at Mount Sinai, where Moses built twelve pillars for the twelve tribes of Israel, and they offered there twenty-four bulls corresponding to what was at Sinai (Exodus 24:5): ״ויזבחו זבחים שלמים לה' פרים״." "<b>And it is possible</b> that they were twenty-four, this corresponding to the left-sided host, which is twenty-four names, as I wrote in the priestly blessing — for Scripture did not state how many they were. And the fact that they also offered sixty rams, sixty goats, sixty lambs — you already know that the sixty rungs correspond to six extremities, ten for each extremity; therefore they offered sixty corresponding to the sixty at Sinai (ibid.) and the seventy elders of Israel, and he added ten corresponding to the seventh extremity, which is holiness. And just as it says here ״ובבא משה אהל מועד לדבר אתו״, corresponding to it at Sinai (ibid. 34) ״ובבא משה לפני ה' לדבר אתו״ ״ויסר את המסוה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:42.520106090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}